{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed for review as Gerrit change 1383 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1383).\n\nFix widens rebar search to match by identifier: reducer/search.py::_haystack now folds in ticket_id, alias, and a new optional jira_key field (all lowercased, single substring path). The reducer stays pure — the caller _engine_support/reads.py::search_state builds a ticket_id->jira_key map once from the binding store reverse index (new _ids.py::binding_jira_key_map, sharing the JSON loader _load_binding_reverse with _resolve_via_binding_store) and annotates each state before calling search_states. Matching is case-folded on both sides so 'search REB-1654' and 'search reb-1654' both surface the bound ticket, mirroring 'show'. Tests: tests/unit/test_search_identifiers.py (pure search_states units incl. case-insensitivity + no-leak) and two integration tests in tests/interfaces/queries/test_ws5a_search.py (ticket_id/alias and bound Jira-key at the CLI seam); all RED-first on origin/main. make lint + make typecheck green; touched files well under the 800 LOC cap. Not closing pending Verified +1 (green CI) and LLM-Review +1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785867820690086001,"uuid":"11adfcf6-87d4-478c-a51d-42fd996fe66e"}